# allowed actually arrive. On `20260906` a second filter by name inside sow_project.sh discarded an
# allowed room, the projection ran, and sow_witness answered GREEN -- because a room that ships no
# bytes leaks no names (REDS %485). A publish is as wrong when a room is missing as when a name
# leaks, and quieter.
# capability seated 20260906.140000 (REDS %493). The guard reads the SHIPPED side, so it needs a
# projection at `seed/` -- which is gitignored, built by `tools/s/sow.rish`, and therefore absent
# from every fresh clone. Rostered `tier lap` with no capability it went red on this tree's first
# cold pass after landing, and a red guard withholds the roster receipt, so `--scoped` refuses and
# every ship pays a FULL cold pass every lap: 778s measured here. The scan's own refusal is right
