# said nothing -- one observation carrying two claims (whether a rota was read, whether it was
# recorded), which is the single-stranded braid. The field existed in practice and in no law until
# that day. REPORTED, never gated: a lap that legitimately did no rota read is indistinguishable
# from one that skipped it, and a gate that cannot tell them apart reds on honest work.
# capability seated 20260907.003211. REPAIRED `20260907.114500`: the guard counted TODAY's logs and
# nothing else, so between 00:00 and the day's first COMMITTED log there was nothing to count and
# its scan refused -- right about the corpus (REDS %170) and wrong about the subject, which made an
# ordinary daily state read as a fault. Measured at 00:12 on `20260907`, the first cold pass of a
# day answered `guards_red=2` on one root: this guard, and `standing_equipment` reading its own
# roster's red. A red guard withholds the roster receipt, so `--scoped` refuses and every ship pays
# a FULL cold pass -- daily, fleet-wide, and healing itself an hour later, which is worse than a
# standing red because it looks like somebody's fault and then vanishes. The scan now falls back to
# the newest shelf that HOLDS a corpus, at most seven shelves back, and prints `day_source=` so an
# open-day reading and a fallback reading are told apart; a day a caller NAMES still refuses.
guard rota_declared
path tools/r/rota_declared_witness.rish
tier lap
capability day_shelf
