# convergence_census -- the tree's own idempotence claim, counted. `what-brix-infuse-is` states
# `infusion(world') -> world'`, and a tool that fails it corrupts on its SECOND run, which is what an
# unattended loop performs at three in the morning. Re-run `20260908.190452`: **10 candidates, 3
# proven**, and the census's own header names some of the ten as libraries or a remote-reading scan
# rather than writers. REPORTED, never gated -- a one-shot publisher has nothing to converge and no
# reading here tells it from a tool that never checked. The denominator was wrong FIVE times: 392
# counting pen writes, 1200 when the census read its own bound as a measurement, 30 counting
# controls, 7 counting non-writers, and 10 admitting the exec-bit write idiom it had been blind to.
# A count this unstable is why the seat's own page says to RUN it rather than read it.
#
# AND THE NUMERATOR WAS WRONG ONCE, in the other direction (`20260908.190452`): it greped every
# tracked path holding the tool's stem, the tool ITSELF included, on any line comment or not, so a
# tool writing `Idempotent: a second run changes nothing` in its own header certified itself. Two
# of the five did exactly that. The census header had stated the rule correctly all along --
# *inside a check rather than a comment* -- and nothing read it. Proven fell to **3 of 10**, and
# the control runs the elder numerator over the same plant to prove the repair moved something.
#
# AND THEN THE NUMERATOR GREW A SECOND SOURCE (`20260908.215031`), because a proof that runs every
# lap was invisible to it. `convergence_tree_prove_witness.rish`, rostered below, proves
# `tools/fixtures/r/reds_ledger_headline_write.sh` converges -- the writer `tools/hooks/pre-commit`
# runs on EVERY commit -- and that tool stood in the unproven column, since only a SIBLING
# assertion counted. A tool is proven now when a runner that is not the tool names it and a
# convergence prover on one non-comment line, and the split is printed:
# `proven_by_sibling_assertion` says a hand wrote a check, `proven_by_prover_run` says somebody ran
# the question. Proven reads **4 of 10**. Six control legs prove it from both sides, the elder
# numerator among them.
guard convergence_census
path tools/c/convergence_census_witness.rish
tier lap
seated 20260907.234808

