guard tame_style_check
path tools/t/tame_style_check.rish
seated 20260707.164612
tier lap       # authored Rye style, named on touch by the same

# THE THREE TAME GUARDS THE LAW PAGES NAME AND NO ROSTER HEARD, seated 20260908.111848.
# `context/TAME_CORE.md` closes on a section titled "The checkable surface (the audit runs these)"
# and names five tools. Four of the five reached a lap only because somebody rostered them one at a
# time for their own reasons; the fifth, `rune_assert_sweep`, was rostered by nobody. The runner the
# page names for all five -- "the TAME Guidance Audit Quest" -- appears in exactly one place in the
# living tree, which is the sentence that names it. `context/TAME_GUIDANCE.md`'s own lint table
# names two more, `opening_lines_witness` and `tame-check`, and neither stood here either;
# `tame-check` is the tool that table cites for FIVE separate rules, unqualified assert among them.
#
# ALL THREE ARE GREEN AT HEAD and have been unheard since they were seated -- `tame-check` and
# `opening_lines` since the parity chapter, `rune_assert_sweep` since `20260810`. Nothing was
# broken; nothing was listening either, which is the second half of this file's own opening law.
#
# `unheard_guard` COUNTED THEM AND COULD NOT NAME THEM. All three stand inside its reading -- one
# in `unheard`, two in the 405 `unnamed_runners` -- under ceilings of 1,108 and 405. An aggregate
# ratchet answers "how many runners does no lap reach"; it cannot answer "is the tool this law page
# declares as its checkable surface one of them". Two questions, one number, and only the first
# was being asked.
#
# WHAT EACH ONE ACTUALLY READS, written here so a green never reads wider than it is. The TAME
# rooms in `tools/fixtures/t/tame_style_rooms.txt` hold 1,126 authored `.rye` files, 1,073 of which
# import std and are therefore hosted. At the seating: `opening_lines` read 25 hand-named files and
# said "all 25 hosted files"; `tame_check` reads 17; `rune_assert_sweep` gates 12 hand-named cores.
# Each is a regression guard over its own list rather than a reading of the tree, and a hand list
# cannot grow with the tree -- the same shape `tally_caller_map` was repaired for on `20260908`.
# Measured at the seating over the whole roster: 123 of the 1,073 hosted files are missing at least
# one line of the opening triad. Widening the lists is its own lap and was named on the card, not
# taken there: rostering a guard and changing what it reads are two acts, and doing both at once
# means no one can tell which of them moved the number.
#
# THE FIRST OF THE THREE WAS WIDENED `20260908.125347`. `opening_lines_scan.rish` now derives its
# population from the rooms roster rather than an inline list, so it reads 1,073 hosted files rather
# than 24. Its "25" was never a file count at all: the witness printed `length lines result.out`,
# which counted 24 OK lines plus the trailing empty one, and three living pages copied the number
# for a year. Two readings are walls -- `qualified_assert` at zero across all 1,073, and the elder
# twenty-four held clean on all four of their duties, so the widening lowers nothing the narrow list
# had proven. Three are ratchets whose ceilings only fall: 5 files calling `std.debug.print(`, 67
# missing the assert bind, 118 missing the print bind.
#
# `tame_check` TOOK THE SECOND LAP `20260908.133141`, and it found something the first did not.
# Its scan reads the same roster and counts every authored `.rye` rather than only the hosted ones,
# because a tab and a trailing space are faults whichever way a file opens: 1,127 rather than 16.
# Three duties are walls at zero across all of them, each on a looser predicate than the literal it
# replaced -- `std.debug.assert(` at any spacing, `Self = @This()` at any spacing, any tab. The
# fourth found three files the sixteen could not see, and all three are load-bearing: two carry a
# trailing space inside a `\\` multiline string, which is generated Zig and generated Brush rather
# than an untidy source, so they are reported under `trailing_content` and gated nowhere; the third
# is `brushstroke/font8x8_data.rye:35`, the glyph row whose `//` comment IS the space character it
# draws. That one is a ratchet at 1 rather than a named exemption, so naming the glyph in words some
# day lowers the ceiling honestly.
#
# ITS COUNT WAS THE SAME FAULT AS THE FIRST ONE'S. `tame-check` printed `length lines result.out`
# and said "all 17 files" against a list of 16, the seventeenth being the trailing empty line --
# exactly the 25-for-24 above, in the guard standing beside it, found the same day. Two of two
# widened guards had been measuring their own output, which is the argument for widening the third.
#
# `rune_assert_sweep` TOOK THE THIRD LAP `20260908.161651`, and the widening found a boundary rather
# than a count. Its scan derives the same 1,127 authored `.rye`, of which 1,100 carry functions, and
# reads TAME root rule 2 in two halves: 100 function-bearing files carry no `assert(` at all, and
# 101 more assert without naming a single `// invariant:`. Both are ratchets whose ceilings only
# fall, because a wall at zero would ask for two hundred files in one lap. What it found is that the
# elder twelve are NOT a subset of the roster -- `mandate/store.rye`, `mandate/keyed.rye`,
# `kumara/tilak.rye`, `settlement/constellation.rye` and `sundial/sundial.rye` sit in four rooms
# `tame_style_rooms.txt` does not name at all -- so deriving alone would have dropped five gated
# files while the printed population grew a hundredfold. The twelve keep a wall of their own at
# zero, each printed by name.
#
# AND ITS OWN HEADER NAMED A READING IT NEVER MADE, caught `20260908.170042` on the air rota --
# the row that feels along a boundary and presses each post. The scan opened by saying it counts
# "at least one `assert(`, each preceded by a `// invariant:` comment. This scan counts both," and
# both of its readings were FILE questions: does this source assert at all, does it name an
# invariant anywhere. The word the rule turns on is EACH, and no instrument in this tree read it.
# `unnamed_assert` reads it now: 6,619 of 24,495 asserts across the 859 asserting module sources
# name nothing. So 73 percent of ASSERTS are named, while 899 of the 1,100
# function-bearing files -- 82 percent -- already satisfied the file reading beside it.
#
# THE SPLIT IS WHAT MAKES THE NUMBER MEAN ANYTHING. A `*_witness.rye` asserts about another
# program's OUTPUT, so its 2,588 unnamed asserts are correct practice rather than debt -- reported
# here and gated nowhere. Read whole, `glow/` scores 1.1 percent named and reads as the worst room
# in the tree; read on its modules alone it scores 92 percent, and those 2,331 asserts were its
# witnesses all along. A reading that libels a room is a reading of the pattern rather than of the
# tree, which is `tame_style_app_sites`' own finding one room over on the same day.
#
# THE ELDER READING IS A STRICT SUBSET, proven by plant rather than argued: a file counted by
# `invariant_gap` necessarily holds an assert counted here, so the control's case 3 now watches two
# ratchets move together, and case 3b plants inside a file that already carries a comment, the only
# way to move the newer reading alone. A blank line breaks the pairing and a comment block opening
# on the invariant carries the run beneath it -- both shown from the failing side. Control 24 legs
# -> 37. The reading costs 2.5s of a lap pass, one `awk` per batch carrying a single flag forward,
# never one grep per file.
#
# AND ITS FIRST DRAFT PAID DIFFUSER'S TAX. Three greps per file against 1,127 sources is 3,381
# processes and 19.3s; three list-wide `grep -l` readings plus `comm` set arithmetic is six, and
# returns the same three counts in 237ms. The witness fell 47.4s -> 2.0s with the control included.
#
# `tier lap` for all three, measured on this pier `20260908`: 19,564ms, 401ms, 172ms against a lap
# pass of 1,537s. The first grew 966ms -> 19.6s at the widening, and the scan itself is 1.3s of that
# -- the other 18 is its control, which runs the scan once per planted state across a throwaway pen.
# A control that proves eighteen behaviors is what the widening is worth, and 1.3 percent of a pass
# is what it costs.
guard rune_assert_sweep
path tools/r/rune_assert_sweep.rish
tier lap   # 7.1s (3.0s scan, 4.1s control); 1,127 derived authored files, plus the twelve elder cores by name
seated 20260908.111848

