# THE SAME LAW, ASKED WHILE THE HAND IS STILL HERE. `shell_dialect` above reads every tracked shell
# source and holds five GNU-only families at a ceiling of zero. It is right, and it arrives late: it
# runs inside a roster pass of roughly half an hour, so the lap that breaks a family is structurally
# never the lap that hears it. Measured `20260908` -- two `sed -i` plants landed at 01:59 and were
# first heard at ANOTHER ship's cold open at 02:42, 43 minutes and one ship later, after which two
# hands cured the same two sites in parallel and one cure withdrew whole.
#
# This is rule seven of tools/hooks/pre-commit: the same five families, read off the INDEX at commit
# time. It gates only the families whose tree ceiling stands at ZERO, which it reads from the elder
# rather than respelling -- a ceiling of zero means no lawful site exists, so every staged hit is a
# rise and no author is refused for a line somebody else wrote. Replayed against commit 0f48f2c85 it
# answers `staged_gated_sites=2` and names both the file and the line.

