# scope_trace seated 20260907.081500. THE MAP IS THE ONE BEHAVIORAL CLAIM IN THIS SYSTEM NOBODY
# CHECKED. tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_scope_map.sh tells a `--scoped` pass which guards a
# change can reach, and a row naming LESS than its guard gates SKIPS REAL WORK -- the map's own
# header says so, and thirteen such rows were repaired by hand on 20260906. This rung runs a guard
# under `strace -f -y -e trace=openat` and matches its observed read set against its row with the
# same tools/fixtures/s/scope_match.sh the runner skips by, so a gap named here is a skip the runner
# would actually take. Two rows were repaired by running it rather than by reading them the day it
# was seated: `radiant_negation` read 142 files against a row reaching 89, missing `.claude/rules/`
# -- its ENFORCE roster, while the rooms the row DID name are its ADVISORY tier -- and
# `tally_roster` read 844 against 28, missing the build edge. Both reproduce
# external-research/20260907-061951 file for file, on a second tree.
#
# WHAT IS GATED is the CONTROL, never a live gap. A row follows a guard's GATED readings and
# observation cannot tell a gated read from an advisory one, so a gap is a word a hand considers
# rather than a defect this rung declares. Union, never subtract.
#
# `capability trace_instrument` because strace is Linux-only; a bench without it reads its own name
# in `skipped_capability` rather than reddening for a kernel it does not have.
#
# `tier lap` at 4s: the control traces a pen guard whose whole read set is four files, so it costs
# nothing near the 58s a real trace of `tally_roster` takes. Tracing a REAL guard stays a hand's
# command, since its cost is the guard's own cost times 1.1x to 6.7x.
guard scope_trace
path tools/s/scope_trace_witness.rish
tier lap
capability trace_instrument
seated 20260907.081500

