# The desk corpus's own reach, seated 20260907.005950. glow/gen/ holds 352 generated desks and exactly one
# guard runs any of them -- tools/g/glow_run_desk_witness.rish, 1,133 lines naming 218 desks one at
# a time. A hand-written enumeration standing in for a population drifts the moment the population
# grows, and nothing here could see it: 129 runnable desks are run by nothing, 89 of which pass on
# metal today. This row does not run desks -- it reads them, so it costs 9s where the desk witness
# would cost a quarter hour of Zig builds, and it is what makes rostering that witness honest
# later. `tier lap` because it is file reading, and because the reading it holds is a ratchet that
# only works if it is read every lap.
#
# 20260907.020441 -- the 129 split in two. The witness runs every desk it names with ZERO
# arguments, and tools/g/glow_run_worker.sh permits a sample for 94 stems, 46 of them in this room.
# All 46 are uncovered and none is covered, so the boundary was the instrument's shape rather than
# anyone's oversight. Two ratchets now: 83 bare desks that cost one block each, 46 sample-taking
# desks that cost a chosen argument first. The sum is derived from them, so it cannot drift.
#
# 20260907.122532 -- the bare ratchet became a gate at zero, because `covered` learned to read both
# instruments. The derived runner below landed and was rostered, and for one lap this reading went
# on deriving `covered` from the elder hand-written witness alone -- printing 83 desks "run by
# nothing" while a guard on this very roster ran all 83. `covered` is the union of `covered_witness`
# and `covered_runner` now, the runner asked with --list rather than derived a second time. What
# `uncovered_bare` counts is a desk NOTHING runs, which makes it the gate on the two derivations
# agreeing: this scan excludes by the markers' intersection, the runner by their union.
guard glow_desk_reach
path tools/g/glow_desk_reach_witness.rish
tier lap
seated 20260907.005950

# The desk corpus actually RUN, seated 20260907.110022. The reach guard above measures how far the
# hand-written witness reaches; this one runs the room. tools/fixtures/g/glow_desk_run_scan.sh
# derives the bare-runnable set on every pass -- every .glow under glow/gen/ minus those declaring
# they must not run by EITHER marker, minus those the worker will only take with a sample -- and
# lowers, builds and runs all 301 of them. The elder tools/g/glow_run_desk_witness.rish names 218
# in 1,133 hand-written lines and is on no roster, because rostering it would publish a 218-desk
# green as coverage of a 352-desk corpus (REDS %532).
#
# Why a batch is cheaper than the blocks it replaces: tools/g/glow_run_worker.sh rebuilds
# glow/bin/glow_run from glow/glow_run.rye on EVERY invocation, which is correct for a hand running
# one desk and wasteful 301 times over. Measured on this pier 20260907 -- 3.80s per desk through the
# worker, 2.42s of it that rebuild, 1.38s the desk's own lower-build-run. The batch builds the
# compiler once, behind the same directory lock the worker takes.
#
# The failure ceiling stands at 3 rather than 0: three files under glow/gen/ are data fixtures
# rather than desks and carry no marker in either name or head, and giving them one is a language
# custody ruling (REDS %532). Run on metal they refuse in two distinct ways, not one.
#
# `cadence` rather than `lap`: 325s of Zig builds measured under a load of 14 is choir money, and
# the desk room grows by a few files a round.
guard glow_desk_run
