# comlink_glow_tend -- Comlink's payload ceiling, displayed and tied. The vane stood in the shape
# museum with one desk, a dual-stack POLICY, while thirty-five bounds went undisplayed, so the
# widest wire surface in the tree was the least shown. `max_wire_payload` = 340 sizes real
# buffers, gates asserts, and two further bounds derive from it -- and it is DERIVED upstream, as
# `wire_capacity - off_cipher`, where four fifths of the header is decided inside the crypto
# library. It was right by arithmetic rather than by a rule: 188 is 188 only because Ed25519 signs
# in 64 bytes, and the card books Kumara moving to SLH-DSA-SHAKE-256s. Three modules spelled the
# answer as a bare literal and named no upstream room.
#
# The scan compares rooms and carries no value of its own, so an honest raise walks free (control
# case 23). What a scan cannot do is evaluate the library widths, so the tie is handed to the
# compiler: `max_wire_payload <= wf.max_message` at comptime, proven both ways on metal in a
# throwaway pen -- as written it builds, inverted it stops the build. Twenty-six control cases,
# five welcomes and twenty-one refusals. The tie count is a FLOOR, so amphora/ tying its own room
# later is welcomed rather than punished.
#
# `cadence` because two legs reach metal -- the tie probe builds two modules and the desk lowers
# through Glow and builds with the Zig toolchain, the same clock the Glow witnesses beside it
# keep. Measured here `20260830.164837`: 10s whole, of which the pure scan and control are under a second.

guard comlink_glow_tend
path tools/co/comlink_glow_tend_witness.rish
tier cadence
seated 20260830.164837

# comlink_carriage -- what a whole is cut into, and whether the pieces can carry it. Three families
# in this tree cut a whole and carry the pieces, each publishing a whole's ceiling, a piece's size,
# and a piece count -- and the relation `whole <= pieces * piece` was stated in no room, no comment,
# and no guard. It held in all three by arithmetic nobody had written down, and the bead family held
# it by EXACTLY ZERO margin: 512 <= 8 * 64, where the 64 is a chunker tuning constant filed beside a
# hash mask rather than beside a carriage bound. Measured before the guard was written: raising
# `max_resin_bytes` 512 -> 576 and changing nothing else refuses 9 of 3,999 pseudorandom wholes with
# TooManyBeads -- a legal input refused by the module that accepted it two lines earlier, on 1 in 444
# contents, which is why a single-fixture test would ship it. The two mantra/ rooms now carry the
# relation at comptime, and amphora/vessel_fetch_wire.rye tied the third on `20260906`, taking
# ties_wired to 3 of 3. That landing turned the gate over: a FLOOR of two had been single-drop
# detection only while two rooms were tied, so the gate now asks each room for its OWN tie and
# wants all three, and the control's case 19 is Amphora dropping its tie rather than adding it
# (REDS %455). Twenty control cases on real files in a throwaway pen, seventeen
# refusals and three welcomes, and a probe that asks the compiler seven times -- four inverted ties
# and the three plausible real edits that were measured to produce a wrong answer. Measured here
# `20260830.200925`: 12s whole, of which the pure scan and control are under a second. At tier cadence
# because it builds two Rye modules eight times over and lowers a desk through Glow, the same clock
# the Glow witnesses beside it keep.

guard comlink_carriage
path tools/co/comlink_carriage_witness.rish
tier cadence
seated 20260830.200925

# comlink_nesting -- whether a frame this tree sends holds the datagram it seals. Every layer of a
# network stack wraps the layer above it, so each container must hold its own header plus the whole
# payload: `container >= header + payload`. Comlink has two such layers and BOTH stand at zero
# slack, and only one of them is safe. The datagram layer is zero because wire_format.rye DERIVES
# it -- `max_message = wire_capacity - off_cipher` -- so raising the capacity raises the message in
# the same expression. The frame layer is zero because it is SPELLED: `max_frame` is the literal 554
# in comlink/virtio_net.rye, `wire_capacity` is the literal 528 in comlink/wire_format.rye, 554 is
# 12 + 14 + 528 exactly, and a doc comment was the only thing joining them. The two rooms cannot
# import each other -- virtio_net.rye is freestanding and imports nothing, wire_format.rye reaches
# std and kumara -- so the arithmetic had nowhere to live but prose. Measured before the guard was
# written: raising `wire_capacity` 528 -> 576 and changing nothing else still BUILDS GREEN for
# riscv64-freestanding, and the guests' own frame arithmetic run hosted reads `index out of bounds:
# index 602, len 554`. Twenty-seven of fifty-nine guests lay a datagram in at that offset, and
# dg_len is `off_cipher + message.len`, so a short message never reaches the ceiling and a full one
# lands on it exactly -- content-dependent, which is why a fixture carrying a short message passes
# forever. virtio_net.rye publishes `frame_carries` and device_wire.rye evaluates it at comptime.
# Sixteen control cases on real files in a throwaway pen, twelve refusals and four welcomes, and a
# probe that asks the compiler six times -- the tie inverted, the three plausible real edits
# (capacity raised, ethernet header grown a VLAN tag, virtio header widened by a field), and an
# honest raise of `max_frame` that must walk free. Measured here `20260830.204814`: 6s whole, of
# which the pure scan and control are 2s. At tier cadence because the probe builds a Rye module six
# times over, the same clock its carriage sibling keeps.

guard comlink_nesting
path tools/co/comlink_nesting_witness.rish
tier cadence
seated 20260830.204814

