# reasoning did not, and the next lap paid to rediscover it. The gate is `unlanded=0`: a session
# log parked at an open is carried by the worktree, a branch, or a remote-tracking branch. It reads
# the RECORD rather than the box, so it goes green by reading a log back and never by dropping a
# stash. The obvious probe would have been `git log --all`, which reaches refs/stash and reports a
# staged record's own stash index commit as history.
# Widened `20260906.194500` (REDS %510): a record is not the work. The session log is the proxy
# because every lap writes one, and the proxy breaks when a lap's log lands while its code does not
# -- `unlanded=0 verdict=ok` over a box still holding the files. Four stood here across three
# stashes, 258 lines, none of them raising `records` by one. The scan now reads every NON-record
# path too: `orphans` is what nothing outside the box carries, `unread` is what something carries
# and whose stashed EDIT no path probe can judge. Reported rather than gated, because a COUNT does
# not travel between checkouts the way `unlanded=0` does; the round open names both drawers.
guard stash_record
path tools/s/stash_record_witness.rish
tier lap
seated 20260906.073939

