# mantra_multifile -- a second tracked file keeps the first one's history. A commit blob named ONE
# weave for a whole directory, so `cmd_add` diffed the next file against the file before it and
# applied the difference, deleting every line of the earlier one -- while the CLI printed
# `wove 2/2 file(s).` The .brix add-all route is the tool's own advertised way to track a project
# of more than one source, and it fired hardest there. This guard drives the built binary down
# exactly that route and asks the tool the user's question -- does an untouched file read clean --
