# Spool Cloth's name bound, seated 20260831.045858 -- the second half of one room's naming layer arriving
# in the shape museum. Tablecloth's four desks landed 20260829 and 20260830 and the last of them
# left the invitation on its own placard: pond/apps/spool_cloth.rye took the same wall in the same
# shape on the same day. The two modules are housemates rather than neighbours, since
# brushstroke/tablecloth.rye is a symlink into pond/apps/, so this is one room finishing its
# thought rather than a new vane arriving.
#
# The guard is shaped like its sibling: the scan reads the number the desk shows and the number the
# Rye publishes and compares them, holding no value of its own, so raising the bound honestly in
# both rooms walks free -- proven as a welcome beside the refusals rather than assumed.
#
# IT CARRIES TWO READINGS ITS SIBLING DOES NOT, and both were found by reading rather than by
# copying. First, this module reads max_name at TWO call sites: store_large refuses a long name
# with NameTooLong, and parse_manifest refuses a long field with BadManifest -- and the second
# guards an array's end rather than a policy, since a parsed name lands in a fixed [max_name]u8.
# They fire apart, so the control reads the survivor by name while its neighbour refuses. Second,
