# amphora_udp_reuseaddr -- the option one line above the port %485 took back, carried for a reason
# UDP does not have.
#
# WHAT WAS WRONG. `amphora/vessel_fetch_delivery.rye` opened every UDP socket under
# `setsockopt(SO_REUSEADDR)`, the invariant reading *SO_REUSEADDR is what lets a bounded run rebind
# its own port*. That is TCP: a closed TCP socket holds its port in TIME_WAIT and the option binds
# through it. UDP has no TIME_WAIT, so the option bought nothing it was added for -- and what it
# bought instead was a DUPLICATE BIND, two sockets holding one port while the kernel splits the
# datagrams between them with no error either side. The per-tree lock beside it was built to catch
# the collision this option had made silent. REDS `20260906.154105`.
#
# WHY IT GATES SOURCE AND PROBES KERNEL. The source reading (`source_reuseaddr_sites`, zero) is the
# regression guard: it is what keeps a plausible comment from walking the option back in. The
# kernel probe is what makes the repair a measurement -- four binds of one port answering, in
# order, that the stated reason needed nothing, that the collision is nameable without the option,
# that the option is what silenced it, and that a mixed pair still refuses. The probe asks the
# kernel for a FREE port rather than naming one, because a hardcoded probe port is this row's own
# fault one level up, and it never touches Amphora's 38494/38495, so no peer's live exchange is
# disturbed. Where `python3` is absent the probe reports itself absent by name and the source gate
# stands alone -- a guard that cannot run its instrument must not describe its subject (%460).
#
# THE THIRD READING IS A CENSUS AND NEVER GATES. `open_socket` was copied module to module with its
# comment intact, so 19 further modules carry the same call -- 1 comlink, 1 granary, 10 linengrow,
# 7 mantra, every one of them SOCK_DGRAM and not one SOCK_STREAM, counted again on this tree at
# `20260906.200000`. Those files belong to other seats, and a guard that reds Amphora over a module
# in Mantra is a guard the fleet turns off, so the count is printed and the verdict ignores it.
#
# `tier cadence`, AND THE TIER IS THE ONE THING HERE NOBODY HAD MEASURED. This block read
# `tier lap`: 1s, no build until `20260906.200000`, while the row it belongs to was parked. Timed
# on this pier: the scan alone **16.8s**, the control **1m57s** over 32 pens, the witness **2m8s**
# together. All three claims in that sentence were wrong -- it is not 1s, it does build (each pen
# is a tree the scan is run against), and at `tier lap` across eight ships it would spend roughly
# seventeen pier-minutes a fleet lap against a whole-roster average near 7s. So it takes the clock
# `topology_attained` takes for the same reason at 192s. What the cadence costs is honest and
# small: the gate catches a walk-back within five rounds rather than one, on a line no lane is
# currently editing. **The elder claim is this row's own subject one level up** -- a number carried
# for a plausible reason that nobody measured -- which is why it is corrected here with three
# timings rather than quietly restated.
#
# ITS OWN NEXT LAP, named rather than taken: the scan's 16.8s is a whole-tree `find` over every
# `.rye`, and the control pays it again on the legs that read the living tree. `git ls-files` and
# one grep pass would cut it; that is a change to the instrument, and this lap's keystone was
# getting the instrument out of the box at all.

guard amphora_udp_reuseaddr
path tools/am/amphora_udp_reuseaddr_witness.rish
tier cadence
seated 20260906.154105

# amphora_mark_wreck -- the vessel named the wreck rule for eight weeks and kept it nowhere.
#
# WHAT WAS WRONG (`20260907.015042`). `foundations/20260703-202312_the-marked-value.md` vows that
# an unknown mark is refused whole -- *there is no partial trust of cargo whose kind cannot be
# named* -- and hardcodes exactly two roots, the plain-bytes mark and the manifest mark. Pond, one
# of the two sites that page names, kept the vow: `pond/customs.rye` asserts
# `verdict_for_mark("stranger-mark") == .refuse`. Amphora, the OTHER site -- the crossing vessel
# whose shoulder line is the whole image the page is built on -- carried the mark field and checked
# it nowhere. `parse_manifest_line` validated the mark's SHAPE (nonempty, at or under
# `max_mark_len`) and never its IDENTITY, and every reading site threw the parsed entry away:
# `vessel_core.rye:160` and `:167`, `vessel_seal.rye:115` and `:229` each wrote
# `_ = me.parse_manifest_line(...) catch return error.InvalidVessel`, keeping the refusal and
# discarding the mark, while `vessel_fetch_delivery.rye` -- the far side of a UDP fetch, which is
# *receipt* in the vow's own word -- stepped over the token with `_ = parts.next(); // mark`
# without parsing at all. Probed on metal: `plain-bytes`, `manifest`, `zzz-unknown-stranger`, and
# `executable` were all ACCEPTED. The module's own header line claimed `wreck rule` and its
# selftest printed `refuse whole`.
#
# WHY NO GUARD SAW IT. The eight elder amphora witnesses plant six tampers -- an absent season, a
# tampered `seal_cargo`, a truncated vessel, a forged resin body, a torn chunk, a reordered pair --
# and every one is an INTEGRITY plant. Not one plants a TYPE. The mark was the only field of the
# three-field line with no negative case anywhere in the room.
#
# WHY THE REFUSAL HAD TO BE READ BY REASON. Editing a sealed vessel breaks its Kumara signature, so
# a planted stranger refuses either way and the exit code proves nothing about marks. Restoring the
# elder behavior, the planted vessel still refuses -- as `error: VerifyFailed`, the signature, with
# `parse_manifest_line` nowhere in the trace. So a correctly sealed vessel carrying `executable`
# rode straight through, and only a tampered one ever refused. This witness asserts the FRAME:
# `parse_manifest_line` must be what turns it away, which is the one assertion the elder tree fails.
#
# WHAT IT COST TO FIX: nothing real. Measured before the gate went in -- exactly one mark rides in
# this whole tree, `plain-bytes`, six occurrences -- so the two named roots break no vessel that
# exists. The check sits in the parser rather than at five call sites, because a rule written five
# times is a rule four places can forget.
#
# THE CENSUS IN THAT PARAGRAPH WAS SHORT BY TWO, counted `20260908` rather than recalled. Six
# callers route a whole line through the parser, not five: `take_listed_line` at
# `vessel_core.rye:234` is a third site in that roof and was named in neither this note nor the
# contract's own comment. And a SEVENTH reader never reached the parser at all --
# `amphora/src/main.rye:append_cargo_line`, which walks decrypted seal plain into a catalog slot
# and so cannot route a whole line. It carried its own tokenizer and its own mark rule,
# `eql(mark, "plain-bytes")`, NARROWER than the two roots every sibling welcomes: a vessel
# carrying the `manifest` root would have passed six readers and died here as `CargoUnproven`.
#
# WHY IT WAS UNREACHABLE, which is why it stood. That door writes what it reads -- `pour` builds
# the cargo plain with its own `mark_plain_bytes`, seals it, and `restore` opens the same plain
# back -- so no argument, file, or vessel edit puts a foreign mark into the plain without
# breaking the AEAD seal first. A leg that cannot be reached is proven where it lives: the
# reader borrows `mark_verdict` and bounds the mark field ahead of it, so an over-long mark now
# REFUSES rather than tripping that function's own precondition assert, and the written root is
# held against the contract's at comptime. A `couples:` marker was tried first and refused --
# `amphora_bounds_agree` reads a bound's spelled NUMERIC value and answered `marker_on_derived`
# on a string, which is the right refusal and pointed at the better home: a marker is checked
# when a guard runs, a comptime assert every time the door is built. Three legs, each proven to
# BITE -- the elder narrower rule restored in a source pen, the bound line deleted, and a
# divergent literal planted, whose build refusal is asserted to name the comptime tie rather
# than merely to be non-zero. REDS `20260908.004856`. GREEN at 7.4s; still `tier lap`.
guard amphora_mark_wreck
path tools/am/amphora_mark_wreck_witness.rish
tier lap
seated 20260907.015042

