# seat_prompt_figure -- a charter says what a ship is FOR, and a count in it can carry no date.
#
# WHAT WAS MEASURED (`20260907.011258`). A seat prompt is the first thing a ship reads on every lap
# it will ever run -- `tools/f/fleet-loop.sh` prepends the baton to it and hands the pair to the
# agent. Eight live seats, eight prompts, and TWO carried tree measurements: copal's `10 Rye modules
# and 3,861 lines` with `16 witnesses`, and patchouli's `32 Rye modules and 9,175 lines` with `four
# rostered witnesses`. All six had parted from the tree.
#
# THE TWO WAYS A FIGURE GOES WRONG, and this pair showed both. Copal's witness figures were EXACT at
# their seating -- 16 tracked paths named both `amphora` and `witness` on `20260905.164639`, and not
# one stood on this roster -- and went stale on ordinary work, reading 17 with 9 rostered by
# `20260907`. The line figure was wrong the day it was written: `3,861` against the **3,582** the
# room's ten `.rye` paths read at that same commit, and against **4,058** today. A figure nothing
# reads cannot be corrected, only replaced.
#
# THE LAW IS ALREADY SEATED ONE ROOM OVER. This file's own directive on `construction/ITINERARY.md`
# reads *Counts come from the scan, never here*, and Gauge asks every figure to carry unit, date,
# and source. A charter carries none of the three: nothing runs it, and no reader can tell a figure
# written this morning from one written in June. This carries that law to the room beside it.
#
# A RATE IS A LAW; A TOTAL IS A MEASUREMENT. `two asserts a function` is TAME's rule and can go
# stale only on a word, so it is counted under `rates` and excluded -- and PRINTED, because an
# exclusion nobody can see is an exclusion nobody can check. `10 Rye modules` claims what the tree
# holds this morning. That one distinction is the whole discriminator.
#
# THE READING IS A FLOOR, DELIBERATELY. Only nouns that can name a code census are read -- module,
# line, witness, guard, assert, function, scan, control. `files`, `rows`, and `pages` are left out
# because a charter says `read its top three rows` as an INSTRUCTION, and a guard that reds on an
# instruction is a guard somebody turns off. So patchouli's `120 files outside it reaching in` is a
# measurement this scan cannot see, named here rather than hidden.
