# topology_stretch -- whether the diameter a shape PUBLISHES is one a table-free router can reach.
# Its sibling `topology_routing` prices the shared next-hop TABLE at 720 points on four shapes; this
# binds the RULE, on seven shapes across two sizes, and the pair divides the subject rather than
# repeating it. Two of the seven route worse than they walk: the circulant that walks 9 is routed at
# 12 by the better of two rules reading only the two addresses, so three of the five hops it seemed
# to buy are bought by a 719-entry table; and pancake, which beats star on mean at one group and one
# degree, finds a shortest path for 296 of 719 where star finds one for all 719. Bubble-sort is the
# counterweight -- table-free, exactly optimal, and still worse than the torus at 15.
# It also reads its OWN source, refusing when a routing function mentions the breadth-first distance
# arrays -- the one fault no hop count can report, since a rule that consults the table prints the
# table-free answer. `tier lap` because vertex-transitivity is CHECKED rather than paid for: one walk
# stands for 720 once six sources spread by a stride coprime to 720 agree, so scan and control
# together are 29s measured `20260907.095458`.
# Named `topology_stretch` rather than the draft's `topology_routed`, which stood three letters from
# the seated `topology_routing` in a roster of 220 -- a grep that cannot separate two guards is a
# collision whatever the filesystem thinks. It is named for the column it alone reports.

guard topology_stretch
path tools/t/topology_stretch_witness.rish
tier lap
seated 20260907.095458

# topology_relaxed -- what the two families that RELAX the star graph's factorial keep, and what
# they give back. Its sibling `topology_stretch` found the one shape that reaches a low diameter and
# routes optimally with no table, and named that shape's wall in the same breath: a star graph has
# n! vertices, so between 720 and 5,040 points the family offers no size at all while a supervision
# tree takes its member count from its membership. This walks the two doors that paper left open.
# Thirteen (n,k)-star graphs from 120 to 6,720 vertices and four arrangement graphs, each built,
# walked breadth-first, and routed from EVERY vertex by named rules. Eight relaxed sizes stand in
# the window the star family leaves empty, two of them at degree 6, and S(7,4) walks 7 on degree 6
# at 840 points where the best three-ring torus of that size walks 14 and every degree-6 commutative
# shape walks 9 or more. The finding is the RULE: the star's rule read literally is exact at k = n-1
# and short at all eleven sizes below it, a one-step correction reaches the true diameter and leaves
# a residue at two sizes, and a rule choosing by where a symbol's CHAIN ends -- in junk, which is a
# free eviction, or at symbol 1, which wastes a move -- routes every vertex of every size by a
# shortest path. Its two anchors are the sibling's own readings at 720 and 5,040, so a builder that
# had drifted would stop reproducing them rather than print confident numbers about the wrong graph.
# It reads its OWN source too, refusing when a routing function mentions the breadth-first distance
# array -- the one fault no hop count can report. `tier lap`: scan 10s, control 30s, witness 43s
# measured `20260907.111058`, because vertex-transitivity is CHECKED from five spread sources rather
# than paid for, and the control reads its plants at one small size through the scan's `SCAN_SIZES`
# knob rather than at all thirteen.

guard topology_relaxed
path tools/t/topology_relaxed_witness.rish
tier lap
seated 20260907.111058

# topology_occupied -- the free-routing claim meets a real membership. Its sibling
# `topology_relaxed` found a table-free rule that routes every vertex of seventeen graphs by a
# shortest path, and closed by naming its own second falsifier unfired: every reading assumed all
# n!/(n-k)! vertices occupied, and a membership never lands on a falling factorial. This fires it.
# Two (n,k)-star graphs are holed in four named geometries across sixteen configurations, and every
# live pair is routed to three sampled targets by three rules, with stretch measured against a walk
# through LIVE members only. Three readings carry the finding. The published rule, which cannot see
# liveness, loses 390 of 2,391 packets at 95 percent occupancy -- one in six. Filtering by neighbour
# liveness stops every hole loss and starts cycling instead, so what the rule lacks is MEMORY rather
# than a table. And a packet carrying the vertices it has already stood on, retreating one hop when
# every ranked neighbour is dead or visited, delivers every reachable pair of every configuration at
# a maximum packet state of 25 entries on an 840-vertex shape -- bounded by the path, not by the
# membership. The geometry reading is bound from BOTH ends because only one is free: a far-end
# symbol class, 120 of 840, costs zero stretch and does not move the diameter, while a DOOR class of
# the same size splits the shape into four components. That partition read 837 of 837 delivered, so
# the count of pairs it made unreachable stands on the same line -- excluding them silently is how a
# partition reads as perfection. Its anchor is the sibling's own two readings, since this file
# carries its own copy of the builder and a drifted copy would measure the wrong graph. It reads its
# OWN source too, refusing when a routing function mentions the breadth-first distance array,
# INCLUDING on the declaration line -- the control planted it there and the first draft passed.
# `tier cadence`: scan 57s, control 35s, witness 95s measured 20260907.145954 and 125s re-measured
# at the landing 20260907.153000 on the same pier -- report the range rather than the luckier run --
# because every live
# pair of every configuration is routed exhaustively rather than sampled, which is heavy for a lap
# and ordinary for a cadence.

guard topology_occupied
path tools/t/topology_occupied_witness.rish
tier cadence
seated 20260907.145954

# topology_partial -- a membership never lands on a whole class either. Its sibling
# `topology_occupied` found that a whole far-end symbol class of S(7,4) -- 120 of 840 vertices --
# costs nothing measurable while the same 120 scattered cost a sixth of the traffic, and closed by
# naming its own falsifier unfired: a membership landing between whole classes, 800 on 840, leaves
# 40 holes with no class to hide them in. This fires it, and refutes the tidy hypothesis that rode
# on it. The classes NEST -- 840 splits 120, 20, 4, 1, derived by the falling factorial and counted
# by grouping the vertices that share each suffix -- yet the freedom does NOT descend the ladder:
# 42 whole level-2 classes, every one 20 vertices and every one leaving the shape in one piece,
# cost between 3 and 491 lost packets of 9,828. Which whole class is the choice that pays. Two
# findings survive. The leftover addresses are nearly free: at 800 live on 840 an arrangement taken
# in far-end-major order loses 429 of 9,588 against 1,156 scattered, and two holes more than a
# whole class can hold cost 457 rather than 429 -- a rounding error rather than a cliff. And the
# SAME contiguous run partitions or does not depending which end of the address is significant:
# 20 holes of S(6,3) taken door-major leave three components and 600 unreachable pairs, where the
# same 20 taken far-end-major leave one component and an unmoved diameter. The naive heuristic --
# keep the holes inside one class, taken door-major -- reads WORST of the five arrangements, behind
# scattering, so the finding is bound from that end too. One method correction is bound with them:
# targets are sampled from the whole address space and held FIXED across arrangements, because
# scored the sibling's way at three live-sampled targets `class_partial` ranked best of five and at
# fifteen it ranked worst by a factor of fourteen. It reads its OWN source, refusing when a routing
# function mentions the breadth-first distance array, and closes a function body at a column-zero
# comment -- which it learned by refusing itself on its first run over a line of prose describing
# that array while touching none of it.
# `tier cadence`: scan 314s, control 102s, witness 416s measured 20260907.173400 on this pier,
# because every live pair of 117 configurations is routed exhaustively rather than sampled and 42
# whole classes are each emptied in turn, which is heavy for a lap and ordinary for a cadence.

guard topology_partial
path tools/t/topology_partial_witness.rish
tier cadence
seated 20260907.173400

