# A TUTORIAL'S QUOTED OUTPUT IS A CLAIM ABOUT BEHAVIOR, and until this row nothing in the tree read
# one. `qa_report_card` scores Truth by whether cited PATHS resolve, `document_mirror_scan` proves
# two homes hold identical bytes, and a fenced output block holds neither a path nor a mirror -- so
# docs-geode/tutorials/the-first-hour.md quoted a three-line ending for its toolchain fetch where
# the command prints four, and the page read Truth 100 the whole time it was wrong
# (20260909.174000). This runs the command above each quoted block and compares. It reads the
# convention the docs-geode room already writes -- an `sh` fence, then an unlabelled fence -- which
# is 6 of the 17 `sh` fences across its 38 tracked pages. WHAT RUNS is narrow on purpose: one plain
# invocation of `rishi/bin/rishi` or `sh` naming a TRACKED script, no redirect, pipe, semicolon,
# ampersand, backtick, dollar or glob. The test is on what EXECUTES rather than on what it is
# handed, so the demos page keeps its deliberately stale resolver argument and still checks. A fence
# that makes a directory or names a script the reader writes is HELD, a ratchet at 2. A block that
# honestly moves declares itself -- `<!-- volatile: why -->` above its fence -- reports, and never
# gates; a reasonless declaration excuses nothing. NOT `docs_command_path`, one row up, which proves
# a printed path RESOLVES: a page can name paths that all resolve and still promise output no
# command produces. `tier lap` at a measured 1.0s: it runs four short commands, and the fault it
# catches is spent by a reader on their first hour.
guard tutorial_output
path tools/t/tutorial_output_witness.rish
tier lap   # 1.0s; 6 pairs read, 4 run, 20 control checks with 5 refusals bitten and lifted
seated 20260909.235500

# self_matching_assert reads the command FORM and the output channel before gating an operand
# match. A simple default-stdout run carrying one literal path is gated; options, stderr,
# compounds, other utilities, and unresolved bindings stay REPORTED, since a label is not a
# reading -- `stat --format=%s path` prints the size alone and names no operand (`%685`).
# `lap` rather than `cadence`: the scan is 1.3s over 2,456 runners and the control 16s, and the
# corpus it reads is every tracked runner, which any lap may add to.
guard self_matching_assert
path tools/s/self_matching_assert_witness.rish
tier lap
seated 20260910.022156

# THE COUNT IN FRONT OF THE BYTE CEILING. A module writing items into a fixed buffer can name two
# maxima -- how many items it carries, and how many bytes it has -- and only one of them is real.
# The encoder decides which, never the declaration. `mantra/recall_tablecloth_query_wire.rye`
# declares `max_wire_hits = 8` six lines above `max_wire_payload = 340`, where one hit at maximum
# name lengths encodes to 119 bytes, so the attainable count is 2. Its sibling
# `recall_sync_wire.rye` declares 8 entries against the same payload where one worst-case entry
# costs 676 bytes -- attainable count zero, under every input. Both were found by hand a lap apart
# (20260909.213236, 20260910.001454), and a lantern that fires twice becomes a loom. Census and
# arithmetic: external-research/20260910-001454_the-count-in-front-of-the-byte-ceiling.md.
#
# THE CLASS IS QUIET, which is why it wants an instrument rather than another hand. A bound too
# SMALL refuses honest work and is found within a day. A count too LARGE refuses nothing, passes
# every test built from short names, and reports its wrong number to every reader who asks.
#
# IT REACHES THE TREE where the hand reached four modules: 29 distinct tracked sources declare both
# shapes, against the 4 the hand-walked census over mantra, caravan, tally and aurora could see.
#
# AND IT DOES NOT JUDGE, which is the finding this guard was built out of. Four lexical
# discriminators were measured against the four cases the paper walked, and every one leaked --
# names in one file (48 candidates, 2 real), names in one function (admits `recall_lap1`, two
# independent guards three lines apart), the byte name checked after a loop (admits
# `glow_storage_scope`, a per-item check inside a loop), and the byte name checked against a
# variable the loop advances (admits it again, on a partial field-name match). The real test is
# whether the loop ACCUMULATES into the bounded buffer, which is dataflow rather than text. A guard
# that guessed would red on honest work and be turned off. So it asks the file to answer instead --
# one `// ceilings: independent|derived|literal` line -- which is the move `declared_ceiling` makes
# for a page and `tutorial_output` for a command: where a judgment cannot be mechanized, mechanize
# the DECLARATION of it. ONE GATE at zero, a verdict no tool can read. TWO RATCHETS that only fall:
# `pairs_undeclared` 25, which every file leaves on the lap a hand touches it, and `pairs_literal`
# 2, the real unrepaired class. A DERIVED ceiling leaves the population by construction, so the
# repair is rewarded by the reading rather than merely permitted -- which is why `caravan/`, whose
# rung bounds are chained, is absent for the right reason. `tier lap` at a measured 3.4s: two
# batched greps over 1,964 sources, then 29 files read again.
guard ceiling_pair
path tools/c/ceiling_pair_witness.rish
tier lap   # 3.4s; 29 pairs read, 14 control behaviors with 5 refusals bitten and lifted
seated 20260910.020000
